<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Spanish War (1635–1659)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1635–1659</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Spanish War was fought from 1635 to 1659 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It began when France under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardinal-richelieu">Cardinal Richelieu</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, continued after the Peace of Westphalia, and was ended by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-pyrenees">Treaty of the Pyrenees</a> (1659), which gave France <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a> and Artois and marked the passing of dominance in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from Spain to France.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-spanish-war-1635-1659.jpg" alt="Franco-Spanish War (1635–1659)" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Habsbourg-1700.png: Katepanomegas derivative work: Alphathon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Habsburg_dominions_1700.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
